More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (401–410)
401. Insecure API Key Transmission
API Key Exposure
API keys are transmitted without proper encryption or appear in client-side code.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
402. Improper Redirect Validation
Open Redirect Vulnerability
Applications redirect users to attacker-controlled websites due to weak validation.
💰 Typical payout: $100 – $2,000
403. Insufficient Password Complexity Enforcement
Weak Password Policy
Applications allow weak passwords that attackers can easily brute-force.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
404. Improper Use of Cryptography
Cryptographic Implementation Weakness
Applications use outdated encryption algorithms or weak implementations.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
405. Improper Access Control on API Resources
API Resource Authorization Bypass
Attackers can access API resources belonging to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
406. Unprotected WebSocket Channels
WebSocket Security Misconfiguration
WebSocket channels allow unauthenticated users to interact with backend systems.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
407. Insecure Storage of Authentication Tokens
Token Storage Vulnerability
Authentication tokens stored in insecure locations such as local storage.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
408. Improper Input Parsing
Input Parsing Vulnerability
Applications incorrectly parse user inputs, leading to security bypass.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $4,000
409. Sensitive Data Exposure via API Responses
API Response Data Exposure
APIs reveal confidential information such as internal IDs or user data.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
410. Improper File Path Validation
File Path Manipulation
Applications fail to validate file paths properly, allowing access to restricted files.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
